{"id": "EUVD-2026-97584", "enisaUuid": "160b03d6-d8ce-3c98-9a78-76696db91a29", "description": "ImageMagick before 6.9.13-57 and 7.x before 7.1.2-32 contains a type confusion flaw in the INFO, JSON and YAML encoders, where an internal method receives a pointer of an unexpected type when writing an image in a compressed format. An attacker who can cause such an image write can trigger a SIGABRT or SIGSEGV, crashing the process and causing denial of service.", "datePublished": "2026-10-12T16:04:45", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T02:37:19", "baseScore": 2.0, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:P/PR:L/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/security/advisories/GHSA-8xmr-6q99-c4x8", "https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/commit/af7b85012e62fa65393277790b96c56a98d882b6", "https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick6/commit/a17cfd15af1038e3ef179016b41ad88e936b4487", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/imagemagick-before-6.9.13-57-and-7-x-before-7.1.2-32-undefined-behavior-in-info-json-and-yaml-encoders"], "aliases": ["GHSA-7vwq-g262-xfgj", "CVE-2026-109282"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.11, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "9c316c03-0365-3c76-b67b-50ca4ba33c75", "product": {"name": "ImageMagick", "vendor": {"name": "ImageMagick"}}, "product_version": "7.0.0-0 <7.1.2-32"}, {"id": "a0ec5b39-88f7-32e1-a577-3dd0e77e9e00", "product": {"name": "ImageMagick", "vendor": {"name": "ImageMagick"}}, "product_version": "0 <6.9.13-57"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "fae51862-270f-31bb-97fb-1f03e3025ab3", "vendor": {"name": "ImageMagick"}}], "isExploited": false}